course: dictionary
lesson: 14001
title: Loyally: staying on someone's side
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Loyally» tells you how someone does something. It means in a faithful way, staying on someone's side and not letting them down. When a friend helps you through a hard time, they are acting loyally.
explain: «The dog waited loyally by the gate every day for his owner to come home.» The dog did not wander off, even when the day was long and cold. Waiting so faithfully shows he stayed true to his owner, so loyally means faithfully.
explain: «Sam stood loyally by his friend when everyone else laughed at her.» Sam did not join in. The word «loyally» tells you he stayed on her side and did not let her down. Check your meaning by swapping in «faithfully»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
explain: In stories, loyal friends keep helping even when it is hard. The Rat, Mole and Badger loyally help Toad even when he is foolish. They keep helping because they care about him, not because it is easy.
fact: Loyally is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Loyally» means in a faithful way, staying on someone's side and not letting them down.
fact: «Loyal» is the adjective: a loyal friend stays faithful when things get tough.
fact: Loyalty is the noun: it means being faithful to a person, team or cause.
fact: Fans can support their team loyally, even when the team keeps losing.
exercise: «The dog waited loyally by the gate for his owner every day.» What does loyally mean? | In a hurry and noisy | *In a faithful way, staying on his owner's side | Sadly, with his tail down | Quickly, so the day went fast
exercise: «Sam stood loyally by his friend when everyone else laughed.» What does Sam do? | *Stays on his friend's side and does not let him down | Forgets his friend's name | Laughs louder than everyone else | Walks away quickly
exercise: Fans cheer for their team loyally, even when it loses. Find and copy the word that tells you how the fans cheer. | fans | team | match | *loyally
test: The Rat, Mole and Badger loyally help Toad even when he is foolish. What does loyally mean here? | Quickly, so the job is done fast | Angrily, shouting at Toad | Unfairly, with no care for Toad | *Faithfully, staying on Toad's side even when he is foolish
test: Which word is closest in meaning to loyally? | *Faithfully | Quietly | Nervously | Rudely
exam: Which sentence uses loyally correctly? | The sun set loyally behind the hill | The cup of tea was loyally hot | The bus was loyally late | *Kai stayed by his sister loyally when she was ill
